---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={"Optional Vertical Tabs Without a Second Interface | Blanc Browser"}
  description={"Switch Blanc to an optional vertical tab rail when a persistent overview helps — resizable, instant, and the island stays your only address and command surface."}
  path="/features/vertical-tabs"
  page="feature-vertical-tabs"
  current="features"
  ogDescription={"Move tabs to a resizable left rail without reloading the page or adding a second browser interface."}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://blancbrowser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Features","item":"https://blancbrowser.com/features"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Vertical tabs","item":"https://blancbrowser.com/features/vertical-tabs"}]}
</script>

<main class="feature-page feature-detail-page">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/features">features</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">vertical tabs</span></nav>
  <section class="feature-hero feature-hero--detail feature-hero--text" aria-labelledby="vtabs-title"><p class="section-kicker">room for a list</p><h1 id="vtabs-title">A tab rail when you want one. The island either way.</h1><p>New in Blanc 1.0: move your tabs to a resizable left rail for a persistent overview — without reloading the page or adding a second browser interface.</p></section>
  <figure class="product-capture feature-capture">
    <div class="demo-stage island-figure island-figure--rail" role="img" aria-label="Blanc's optional vertical tab rail: a slim left column listing open tabs beside the page, with the resting island above.">
      <div class="demo-rail" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="rail-row"><span class="fav"></span><span class="ttl t1"></span></div>
        <div class="rail-row cur"><span class="fav"></span><span class="ttl t2"></span></div>
        <div class="rail-row"><span class="fav"></span><span class="ttl t3"></span></div>
        <div class="rail-row"><span class="fav"></span><span class="ttl t4"></span></div>
        <div class="rail-row"><span class="fav"></span><span class="ttl t5"></span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo-page" aria-hidden="true"><div class="bar w1"></div><div class="bar w2"></div><div class="bar w3"></div><div class="bar w4"></div></div>
      <div class="demo-island" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="pill">
          <div class="dots"><span></span><span class="cur"></span><span></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>The rail lists every open tab by title while the island keeps navigation, search, and commands in one place.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top" aria-labelledby="vtabs-behavior-title">
    <div><p class="section-kicker">how it works</p><h2 id="vtabs-behavior-title">One switch. No reload. No second address bar.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Switch layouts instantly.</h3><p>Choose View → Tab Layout → Vertical Tabs, or press Command or Control Alt V. The page you are reading stays exactly where it is — nothing reloads.</p></article>
      <article><h3>A rail that fits your session.</h3><p>Every open tab becomes a row with its title, so a wide session stays readable instead of shrinking into dots. Drag the rail's edge to the width you want; Blanc remembers it on this device.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Still one island.</h3><p>The rail is an overview, not a second interface. Searching, navigating, and commands stay on the island, so nothing you have learned about Blanc changes.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="vtabs-note-title"><p class="section-kicker">good to know</p><h2 id="vtabs-note-title">The island layout stays the default.</h2><p>Blanc starts in its island layout, and vertical tabs are a choice you make per device — the setting never syncs, so a rail on your desktop does not rearrange your laptop. Switch back the same way you switched in.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/island" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="vertical-tabs" data-cta-position="truth-note">Meet the island <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside>
  <section class="feature-close" aria-labelledby="vtabs-close-title"><p class="section-kicker">ready when you are</p><h2 id="vtabs-close-title">Keep the overview. Lose the clutter.</h2><a class="cta" href="/download" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="vertical-tabs" data-cta-position="feature-close">download blanc</a></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
